A||||5||Homicidal||Subwoofer noise/picking of sound of the engine??????||||5||
Z||000000||Homicidal||06-23-2000||03:18 PM||||I don't get it, sometimes when I turn my car on, my subwoofer starts to pick up the current of the engine and you can HEAR it in the subwoofer!  Why is this?  I am thinking it's with the ground cable. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||06-23-2000||03:30 PM||||It's either the ground cable or the cables to the sub amp have a bad sheild. Make sure you use a good pair of RCA cables. Also make sure the case of the amp isn't touching car frame. This will create a ground loop causing noise to be picked up/generated.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Homicidal||06-23-2000||03:35 PM||||RCA cables are good, but the amp is touching the car.  I will move it and then try it.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||gkozlov||06-23-2000||04:10 PM||||Are you reffering to the Altec Lansing. If so you need to go get a noise filter from Radio Shack. They are about ten bucks. Mine works great and it solved my hissing.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||06-23-2000||04:32 PM||||Bad Ground.||||reg||14
Z||000005||BroCar 87||06-23-2000||05:15 PM||||Homicidal, That engine noise is the most COMMON noise in system set-ups. The main things to check are the GROUNDS FIRST, then your RCA cables, and then your power wires. <BR>I had the same problem with my amp last week. Come to find out my power wire to the battery was loose. I tightened it up and it stopped the humming. It was barely loose too, so it didn't humm all the time.<BR>Hope that helps!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
